6. Full Evidence Aggregation Specification
6.1 Evidence Aggregation Schema
The evidence aggregation schema defines the structure of an evidence aggregation deposit.

It has the following fields:

aggregation_id. A string. Required.

aggregation_name. A string. Required.

claim_id. A string. Required.

claim_description. A string. Required.

source_app. An enum. Required. The values are physics_knowledge_library, replication_tracker, anomaly_register, medical_claim_verifier, psychological_effect_registry, climate_attribution_registry, historical_claim_registry, mathematical_conjecture_registry, other.

evidence_sources. An array of evidence objects. Required.

aggregate_strength. An enum. Required. The values are strong, moderate, weak, inconclusive.

aggregate_uncertainty. An object. Required. It contains confidence_interval and standard_error.

aggregation_method. An enum. Required. The values are fixed_effect, random_effects, Bayesian, other.

heterogeneity. An object. Required. It contains I_squared, tau_squared, Q_statistic, and sources.

bias_assessment. An object. Required. It contains publication_bias, selection_bias, measurement_bias, and other_bias.

gap_analysis. An object. Required. It contains missing_evidence_types and recommendations.

sensitivity_analyses. An array of sensitivity analysis objects. Optional.

related_aggregations. An array of aggregation relations. Optional.

provenance. An object. Required.

work_reference. A string. Optional.

full_pipeline_result_reference. A string. Optional.

null_model_result_reference. A string. Optional.

verification_result_reference. A string. Optional.

replication_tracker_reference. A string. Optional.

keywords. An array of strings. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

moderation_status. An enum. The values are pending, approved, rejected.

version. An integer.

supersedes. A string. Optional.

superseded_by. A string. Optional.

Each evidence object has:

evidence_id. A string.

evidence_description. A string.

evidence_type. An enum. The values are study, dataset, replication, meta_analysis, critique, observation, other.

source_reference. A string.

source_app. A string. Optional.

effect_size. An object. Optional. It contains value and units.

confidence_interval. An object. Optional. It contains lower and upper.

p_value. A number. Optional.

sample_size. An integer. Optional.

quality. An enum. The values are high, moderate, low, very_low, not_assessed.

weight. A number. Optional.

independence. An enum. The values are independent, partially_independent, shared_assumption, unknown.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each sensitivity analysis object has:

analysis_id. A string.

analysis_description. A string.

analysis_method. An enum. The values are leave_one_out, quality_weighted, outliers_removed, different_model, other.

analysis_result. An object. It contains aggregate_strength, aggregate_uncertainty, and notes.

Each aggregation relation has:

relation_id. A string.

related_aggregation_id. A string.

relation_type. An enum. The values are same_claim, same_source_app, supersedes, superseded_by, related, independent.

relation_note. A string. Optional.

