12. Validation Engine Design
The system validates the following.

Validation 1. Aggregation validity. Every aggregation is validated against the schema.

Validation 2. Referential integrity.

Validation 3. Version chain acyclicity.

Validation 4. Work resolution.

Validation 5. Full-pipeline result resolution.

Validation 6. Null-model result resolution.

Validation 7. Verification result resolution.

Validation 8. Replication tracker record resolution.

Validation 9. Provenance completeness.

Validation 10. Audit completeness.

Validation 11. Moderation completeness.

Validation 12. Method consistency. The aggregation method must be consistent with the evidence.

Validation 13. Effect size consistency. The effect sizes must be consistent with the units.

Validation 14. Strength consistency. The aggregate strength must be consistent with the effect size and the uncertainty.

Validation 15. Heterogeneity consistency. The heterogeneity must be consistent with the evidence.

Validation 16. Bias consistency. The bias assessment must be consistent with the evidence.

Validation 17. Gap consistency. The gap analysis must be consistent with the evidence.

